      "y": -26.8,
      "z": 79.4,
      "excerpt": "# Quarterly Business Review\n\nThe Quarterly Business Review (QBR) is our most important strategic meeting at Bloom & Brew. It's where we step back from daily operations and assess the health and direction of the business.\n\n## QBR Agenda Template\n\n### 1. Financial Review (30 min)\n- [[Revenue Streams]] performance vs. targets\n- [[Budget Planning]] actuals vs. plan\n- [[Pricing Strategy]] margin analysis\n- Cash flow and runway\n\n### 2. Operations Review (20 min)\n- [[Inventory Management]] efficiency and waste metrics\n- [[Facilities Maintenance]] updates and needs\n- [[Supplier Relationships]] status and any issues\n- [[Shift Scheduling]] coverage and labor costs\n\n### 3. Marketing Review (20 min)\n- [[Social Media Strategy]] metrics and growth\n- [[Email Marketing]] performance\n- [[Seasonal Campaigns]] results (if applicable)\n- [[Partnership Opportunities]] pipeline update\n\n### 4. Team Review (15 min)\n- [[Team Roster]] changes and hiring needs\n- [[Training and Onboarding]] progress\n- [[Employee Wellness Program]] check-in\n- [[Customer Feedback Program]] trends\n\n### 5. Strategic Planning (30 min)\n- [[Growth Roadmap]] progress\n- [[Loyalty Program]] enrollment and engagement\n- [[Product Catalog]] updates\n- New initiatives and experiments\n\n### 6. Action Items (15 min)\n- Review previous quarter's action items\n- Assign new action items with owners and deadlines\n\n## Logistics\n\n- Held on the first Saturday after quarter end\n- Studio closed for half day (morning session)\n- All [[Team Roster]] leads attend; summary shared with full team\n- Catered lunch afterward as a team appreciation moment\n\n## Documents\n\nAll QBR presentations are archived in our Google Drive. The [[Tech Stack and Tools]] document has access details.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83e\udde0 J.A.R.V.I.S. Expanded Understanding & Neural Synthesis\n* **Core Semantic Insight:** This note codifies the rhythm of executive governance for Bloom & Brew, transforming abstract business management into a rigorous, synchronized ritual that safeguards both financial solvency and operational alignment.\n* **Operational Context:** When QBR preparations or reviews are initiated, I will proactively compile cross-domain metrics\u2014synthesizing financial actuals, inventory efficiencies, and marketing yields\u2014to streamline your strategic analysis and ensure zero administrative friction.\n* **Cross-Domain Links:** The framework serves as a central nervous system bridging *Finance* (runway, budgeting), *Operations* (inventory, labor), *Marketing* (campaign yields, partnerships), and *Products* (catalog updates, loyalty metrics), providing a unified intelligence feed for holistic enterprise oversight.\n"
