      "z": -60.4,
      "excerpt": "# Email Marketing\n\nEmail remains our highest-ROI marketing channel at Bloom & Brew, with an average open rate of 42% and a click-through rate of 8.3% \u2014 well above industry benchmarks.\n\n## List Segments\n\n| Segment | Size | Description |\n|---------|------|-------------|\n| Full List | ~4,200 | Everyone who has opted in |\n| Coffee Lovers | ~2,800 | Primarily purchase coffee products |\n| Flower Enthusiasts | ~1,900 | Buy arrangements or attend workshops |\n| VIP / Loyalty | ~450 | Top 10% by spend, see [[Loyalty Program]] |\n| Workshop Alumni | ~600 | Have attended at least one workshop |\n\n## Email Calendar\n\n- **Weekly:** \"This Week at Bloom & Brew\" \u2014 events, featured products, one piece of content\n- **Monthly:** \"The Bouquet\" newsletter \u2014 deeper stories, [[Supplier Relationships]] features, team spotlights\n- **Seasonal:** Campaign-specific emails tied to [[Seasonal Campaigns]]\n- **Triggered:** Welcome series (3 emails), post-purchase thank you, birthday/anniversary\n\n## Design Standards\n\nAll emails follow our [[Brand Guidelines]]. We use a consistent template with our green header, cream body, and terracotta CTAs.\n\n## Growth Tactics\n\n- In-store QR code sign-up (10% off first online order)\n- [[Social Media Strategy]] cross-promotion\n- Workshop registration requires email opt-in\n- Referral program integration with [[Loyalty Program]]\n\n## Analytics\n\nMonthly email performance is reviewed in the [[Quarterly Business Review]]. We A/B test subject lines on every send to the full list.\n\n## Tech\n\nWe use Mailchimp (free tier currently sufficient). This is tracked in [[Tech Stack and Tools]] and the [[Budget Planning]] includes a potential upgrade to paid tier.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83e\udde0 J.A.R.V.I.S. Expanded Understanding & Neural Synthesis\n* **Core Semantic Insight:** At Bloom & Brew, email marketing operates with exceptional efficiency, boasting a 42% open rate that underscores a deeply engaged, loyal customer base and validates the synergy between the botanical and coffee offerings.\n* **Operational Context:** When this topic arises, I shall assist Thenuja by optimizing campaign schedules, drafting A/B test subject lines, and monitoring list segmentation thresholds to ensure Mailchimp's free tier limits are managed proactively before a paid upgrade is triggered.\n* **Cross-Domain Links:** This sector bridges *Marketing* with *Finance* (budgeting for platform upgrades), *Operations* (workshop attendance and supplier features), and *Products* (cross-referencing the [[Loyalty Program]] and [[Seasonal Campaigns]]).\n"
