      "excerpt": "# Seasonal Campaigns\n\nSeasonal campaigns are the revenue spikes that fund our quieter months. At Bloom & Brew, the intersection of coffee and flowers means we can capitalize on holidays that other businesses can't.\n\n## Annual Campaign Calendar\n\n### Q1\n- **Valentine's Day** (our BIGGEST day) \u2014 \"Love in Bloom\" campaign\n  - Flower arrangement pre-orders start Jan 15\n  - Limited edition rose latte\n  - Couples' arrangement workshop\n  - Revenue target: 3x average week (see [[Revenue Streams]])\n\n- **Mother's Day** (May, but planning starts Q1) \u2014 \"For the Woman Who Blooms\"\n  - Second biggest revenue event\n  - Gift bundles: flowers + coffee subscription\n  - Brunch pop-up collaboration\n\n### Q2\n- **Summer Sipping Series** \u2014 Iced coffee flights + summer arrangements\n- **Wedding Season** \u2014 Push [[Product Catalog]] wedding packages\n\n### Q3\n- **Back to School** \u2014 Teacher appreciation bundles\n- **Fall Launch** \u2014 Pumpkin spice + autumn arrangements\n- **Small Business Saturday** prep begins\n\n### Q4\n- **Holiday Collection** \u2014 Wreaths, centerpieces, gift sets\n- **Corporate Gifting** \u2014 B2B holiday packages (see [[Partnership Opportunities]])\n- **New Year** \u2014 Subscription launches for [[Loyalty Program]] members\n\n## Execution\n\nEach campaign gets a brief that includes: goals, [[Budget Planning]] allocation, [[Social Media Strategy]] content plan, [[Email Marketing]] sequences, and in-store merchandising. The [[Team Roster]] assigns a campaign lead for each major event.\n\n## Post-Campaign Review\n\nResults are compiled for the [[Quarterly Business Review]] with lessons learned and recommendations for next year.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83e\udde0 J.A.R.V.I.S. Expanded Understanding & Neural Synthesis\n* **Core Semantic Insight:** At Bloom & Brew, seasonal campaigns represent the financial lifeblood of the enterprise\u2014leveraging the unique dual identity of coffee and floristry to engineer high-yield revenue spikes that subsidize quieter operational quarters, with Valentine's Day acting as the undisputed crown jewel of the fiscal calendar.\n* **Operational Context:** When campaign execution is discussed, I shall maintain active cross-referencing vectors across budgeting, inventory management, and staffing to ensure seamless synchronization from pre-order logistics down to post-campaign analytics for the Quarterly Business Review.\n* **Cross-Domain Links:** This framework heavily integrates with **Finance** ([[Revenue Streams]], [[Budget Planning]]), **Marketing** ([[Social Media Strategy]], [[Email Marketing]]), **Operations** ([[Team Roster]]), and **Products** ([[Product Catalog]], [[Loyalty Program]]), demanding an orchestrated, multi-departmental approach to every holiday rollout.\n"
