      "y": -33.4,
      "z": 66.8,
      "excerpt": "# Inventory Management\n\nEffective inventory management is critical for Bloom & Brew since we deal with two highly perishable product categories: fresh flowers and specialty coffee beans.\n\n## Coffee Inventory\n\n- Green beans are ordered bi-weekly from our [[Supplier Relationships]] partners\n- Roasted beans have a 14-day freshness window\n- We maintain a minimum stock of 20 lbs per variety\n- Reorder triggers are managed through our spreadsheet system (see [[Tech Stack and Tools]])\n\n## Floral Inventory\n\n- Fresh flowers are sourced three times a week from local growers and the wholesale market\n- Seasonal availability drives our [[Product Catalog]] offerings\n- Waste tracking is essential \u2014 we aim for under 8% spoilage\n- Dried flower supplies for our workshop series are ordered monthly\n\n## Storage\n\nThe back room is split into zones: cold storage (flowers, 34-38\u00b0F), cool storage (beans, 60-65\u00b0F), and dry storage (packaging, retail items). The [[Facilities Maintenance]] schedule includes daily temperature checks.\n\n## Counting\n\nFull inventory counts happen every Sunday evening after close. The [[Shift Scheduling]] always assigns two people for this task. Discrepancies over $50 are reported in the [[Quarterly Business Review]].\n\n## Integration with Sales\n\nOur [[Revenue Streams]] analysis shows that inventory turns directly impact margin. The [[Pricing Strategy]] document outlines our markup targets per category.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83e\udde0 J.A.R.V.I.S. Expanded Understanding & Neural Synthesis\n* **Core Semantic Insight:** For Pixel Bloom Studios' hybrid storefront, *Bloom & Brew*, inventory management is not merely a logistical ledger, but a high-stakes calculus of perishability\u2014where the razor-thin margins of fresh botanicals and specialty roasts demand absolute operational precision to prevent fiscal erosion.\n* **Operational Context:** When inventory metrics, waste thresholds, or reorder schedules are queried, I shall synthesize real-time data from your tech stack with strict adherence to temperature thresholds, spoilage caps (<8%), and minimum stock parameters to preemptively flag supply chain vulnerabilities.\n* **Cross-Domain Links:** This operation intersects intimately with **Finance** (impacting margin analysis and QBR discrepancy reporting), **Facilities** (dictating daily thermal calibration), and **Human Resources** (coordinating Sunday evening dual-operator counts via shift scheduling).\n"
