      "y": -52.5,
      "z": -89.4,
      "excerpt": "# Tech Stack and Tools\n\nThis document catalogs all the technology tools Bloom & Brew uses to run the business. We keep it simple and affordable.\n\n## Current Stack\n\n### Point of Sale\n- **Square POS** \u2014 Processes all transactions, tracks basic sales data\n- Integrated with our [[Loyalty Program]] tracking\n- Monthly cost: $0 (free tier + per-transaction fees)\n\n### Communication\n- **Slack** (free tier) \u2014 Team chat, organized by channels (#coffee, #floral, #general, #scheduling)\n- **Google Workspace** \u2014 Email (bloomandbrew.com), Drive for document storage, Sheets for tracking\n- Used for [[Daily Standup Process]] notes and [[Shift Scheduling]] sheet\n\n### Marketing\n- **Mailchimp** (free tier) \u2014 [[Email Marketing]] platform\n- **Canva** (pro, 1 seat) \u2014 Design tool for [[Social Media Strategy]] and [[Brand Guidelines]] assets\n- **Later** (free tier) \u2014 Social media scheduling\n- **Google Business Profile** \u2014 Reviews, local SEO, maps\n\n### Finance\n- **Wave Accounting** (free) \u2014 Bookkeeping, invoicing, [[Budget Planning]] tracking\n- **Square Dashboard** \u2014 [[Revenue Streams]] daily sales tracking\n- **Google Sheets** \u2014 Custom financial models, [[Pricing Strategy]] calculators\n\n### Operations\n- **Google Sheets** \u2014 [[Inventory Management]] tracking, [[Shift Scheduling]]\n- **Google Forms** \u2014 [[Customer Feedback Program]] surveys, workshop sign-ups\n- **Trello** (free) \u2014 Project management for [[Seasonal Campaigns]] and [[Growth Roadmap]] initiatives\n\n### Knowledge Management\n- **Google Drive** \u2014 All documents, [[Training and Onboarding]] materials, [[Quarterly Business Review]] archives\n- **Notion** (free) \u2014 SOPs, recipes, arrangement guides ([[Product Catalog]] details)\n\n## Planned Upgrades\n\n| Tool | Purpose | Monthly Cost | Priority |\n|------|---------|-------------|----------|\n| 7shifts | [[Shift Scheduling]] | $35 | High |\n| Mailchimp Essentials | [[Email Marketing]] upgrade | $20 | Medium |\n| Lightspeed POS | Better [[Inventory Management]] integration | $89 | Low (Phase 2) |\n| Dedicated loyalty app | [[Loyalty Program]] upgrade | $50 | Medium |\n\n## Security & Access\n\n- All accounts use strong passwords + 2FA where available\n- Maya and Jordan have admin access to all systems\n- [[Team Roster]] leads have manager-level access to their relevant tools\n- Shared account credentials stored in a password manager (Bitwarden, free)\n\n## Budget\n\nTotal current tech spend: ~$35/month. Planned upgrades budgeted in [[Budget Planning]] and phased per [[Growth Roadmap]] timeline.\n\n## Training\n\nNew hires are trained on all relevant tools during [[Training and Onboarding]] Week 1. Tool-specific quick reference guides are pinned in the relevant Slack channels.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83e\udde0 J.A.R.V.I.S. Expanded Understanding & Neural Synthesis\n* **Core Semantic Insight:** This infrastructure architecture for *Bloom & Brew* reflects a masterclass in capital efficiency\u2014utilizing a bootstrapped, zero-to-low-cost SaaS ecosystem (Square, Google Workspace, Notion) to orchestrate dual retail operations without bleeding cash, while strategically staging paid upgrades for scalable growth.\n* **Operational Context:** When Thenuja queries operational bottlenecks, inventory anomalies, or software expenditures, I shall cross-reference this stack to recommend immediate automation hacks, troubleshoot permission tiers, or model the financial impact of upcoming migrations like *7shifts* or *Lightspeed*.\n* **Cross-Domain Links:** This document serves as the connective tissue bridging **Products** (inventory and recipes), **Finance** (budgeting and Wave bookkeeping), **Marketing** (Mailchimp and Canva assets), and **Operations** (shift scheduling and onboarding), directly feeding into the broader *Growth Roadmap*.\n"
