      "y": 31.0,
      "z": 100.1,
      "excerpt": "# Employee Wellness Program\n\nAt Bloom & Brew, we believe that happy, healthy team members create the best experiences for our customers. Our wellness program is modest but meaningful.\n\n## Core Benefits\n\n- **Health Stipend:** $100/month health and wellness stipend (gym, therapy, etc.)\n- **Free Drinks:** Unlimited coffee and tea during shifts\n- **Staff Discount:** 50% off all products (see [[Pricing Strategy]])\n- **Flexible Scheduling:** We accommodate school schedules, second jobs, and life events through [[Shift Scheduling]]\n- **Mental Health Days:** 3 additional days per year, no questions asked\n\n## PTO Policy\n\n- Full-time: 10 days PTO + 3 mental health days + holidays\n- Part-time: 5 days PTO + 2 mental health days + holidays\n- PTO requests go through [[Shift Scheduling]] process\n- Blackout dates around major [[Seasonal Campaigns]] (Valentine's Day, Mother's Day, holidays)\n\n## Team Building\n\n- Monthly team outings (budgeted in [[Budget Planning]])\n- Quarterly team dinner after [[Quarterly Business Review]]\n- Annual summer picnic\n- [[Daily Standup Process]] \"kudos\" moment for peer recognition\n\n## Professional Development\n\n- See [[Training and Onboarding]] for certification opportunities\n- Conference attendance for leads (one per year)\n- Book club (current read: \"Setting the Table\" by Danny Meyer)\n\n## Wellness Check-ins\n\n- Monthly anonymous pulse survey (3 questions)\n- Quarterly 1:1 with direct manager\n- Annual comprehensive satisfaction survey\n- Results discussed at [[Quarterly Business Review]] and influence [[Growth Roadmap]] people strategy\n\n## Open Door Policy\n\nMaya and Jordan maintain an open door policy. Any [[Team Roster]] member can schedule time to discuss concerns, ideas, or career goals. We also monitor the [[Customer Feedback Program]] for any mentions of specific team members to address both praise and concerns.\n\n## Future Plans\n\nAs we grow per the [[Growth Roadmap]], we plan to add dental insurance and increase the wellness stipend. This is tracked in [[Budget Planning]] as a future line item.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83e\udde0 J.A.R.V.I.S. Expanded Understanding & Neural Synthesis\n* **Core Semantic Insight:** For Thenuja, the \"Bloom & Brew\" Employee Wellness Program transcends standard HR policy, serving as a foundational cultural blueprint that marries human capital investment with operational resilience\u2014crucial for sustaining service excellence without burning out the talent pipeline.\n* **Operational Context:** When this topic arises, J.A.R.V.I.S. will maintain strict alignment with Bloom & Brew\u2019s cultural standards, dynamically cross-referencing scheduling conflicts, financial constraints, and strategic milestones to ensure that operational demands never inadvertently compromise team welfare or trigger preventable attrition.\n* **Cross-Domain Links:** This policy bridges multiple sectors within the database, tying directly into **Finance** via *Budget Planning* stipends, **Operations** through *Shift Scheduling* and *Training and Onboarding*, and overarching strategic vectors like the *Growth Roadmap* and *Quarterly Business Review*.\n"
